    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44682" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŏlūbĭlis</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		solvo (post-class.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Pass.</i>, <i>that may be loosed</i>
			or <i>taken apart</i>, <i>dissolvable</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pons,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 16, 8, 10</span></i>
			: mundus, Min. Oct. 34: caro, Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 10, 506. —* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>loosening</i>, <i>relaxing</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aër,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
						Aur. Acut. 2, 37, 192</span></i>
			.</div>
